hadiths[19]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1537","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I was serving a drink made from unripe and ripe dates to Abu Ubaidah bin Jarrah, Abu Talha Ansari, and Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with them), when a person came and said: Indeed, alcohol has been declared forbidden. So Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Anas! Get up and break these pitchers. Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I took the pestle used for grinding grain and struck them from below until they broke."
"1538","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever drank alcohol in this world and did not repent from it, he will be deprived of it in the Hereafter."
"1539","Umm al-Mu'mineen Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every drink that causes intoxication is forbidden."
"1540","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was asked about ""bit‘"" (a drink made from honey). He (peace be upon him) said: ""Every intoxicating drink is forbidden."
"1541","It is narrated from Tawus that Abu Wahb Jaishani asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about Bit‘ (a drink made from honey). The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Every intoxicating substance is forbidden.”"
"1542","Abu Juwayriyah al-Jurmi says: Indeed, I am the first Arab who asked Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) about Baadhq, and he was sitting reclining against the Ka'bah. He said: ""Muhammad ﷺ passed away before the (invention) of Baadhq. Whatever intoxicates is forbidden."
"1543","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that every intoxicating substance is wine, and every kind of wine is forbidden."
"1544","It is narrated from Ata bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about Ghabeera, so he (ﷺ) said: ""There is no good in it,"" and he (ﷺ) forbade it. Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) says: Zaid bin Aslam said: ""Ghabeera is a drink made from barley."
"1545","It is narrated from Ata bin Yasar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about Ghabeera, so he (ﷺ) said: ""There is no good in it,"" and he (ﷺ) forbade it. Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Zaid bin Aslam said, ""Ghabeera is a drink made from barley."
"1546","It is narrated from Mahmood bin Labeed Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that when Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Syria, the people of Syria complained to him about the plague and the bad climate, and said: Nothing except wine can keep us healthy. So Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to them: ""You should drink honey."" They said: We do not recover with honey. One man among them said: If we take wine to such a state that its intoxication is gone, what do you say? He replied: ""That is fine."" Then they cooked it over the fire until two-thirds of it evaporated and one-third remained, and they brought it to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) dipped his finger in it, then raised his hand, and it stuck like a string. He said: ""This is talaa (thick syrup), it is like the talaa used for camels."" Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered them to drink it, so Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: By Allah! You have made it lawful. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: ""Never! By Allah! O Allah! That which You have made unlawful, I do not make lawful for them, and that which You have made lawful for them, I do not make unlawful for them."
"1547","Ma'bad bin Ka'b narrated from his mother (who had prayed facing both Qiblahs) that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade making nabidh by mixing two kinds of fruits and said: ""Make nabidh of each one separately."
"1548","It is narrated from Ata bin Yasar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade making nabidh by mixing together dates and partially ripe dates, and by mixing together dry dates and nearly ripe dates."
"1549","Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade making nabidh (fermented drink) in green, white, and red pitchers."
"1550","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not prepare nabidh (fermented drink) in vessels made from gourds or in greased containers."" (Abu Salama said) Then Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: ""You should also avoid green greased jars and vessels made by hollowing out wood."
"1551","Zuhri narrates that I heard Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade making nabidh (fermented drink) in vessels made of gourds and in greased jars."
"1552","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon to the people during a certain expedition. Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: I turned towards him, but before I reached, he (peace and blessings be upon him) had already returned. I asked the noble companions (may Allah be pleased with them) what he had said. They replied that he (peace and blessings be upon him) had forbidden making nabidh (fermented drink) in gourds made from bottle gourd and in oil jars."
"1553","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade making nabidh (fermented drink) in vessels made of gourd and in green, greased jars."
"1554","Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade (making nabidh) in certain vessels, it was said to him that not everyone has a waterskin. Then the Prophet ﷺ permitted (making nabidh) in all jars except the green, oily jar."
"1555","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that Nabidh used to be soaked for the Prophet (ﷺ) in a waterskin; if that was not available, then it would be soaked in a drinking vessel made of stone."
